  "question": {
    "text": "A travelling microscope has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> divisions per <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math> on the main scale while its Vernier scale has total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> divisions and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math> Vernier scale divisions are equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math> main scale divisions, what is the least count of the travelling microscope ?",
